# Frontend and Extension Safety

- Treat all external data as untrusted; validate and escape before rendering.
- Keep extension messaging boundaries explicit (content/background/page bridge).
- Favor progressive enhancement and graceful fallback when APIs fail.
- Keep UI changes accessible (labels, focus order, semantic controls).
- Avoid risky client-side storage of sensitive values.

## Casino & Sweepstakes Domain Invariants

- **Dual-Currency Awareness (SC vs GC):** Sweepstakes casinos (Stake.us, Crown Coins, LoneStar, Real Prize, Chumba, McLuck, Pulsz, WOW Vegas) utilize Sweeps Coins (SC, redeemable 1:1 USD) and Gold Coins (GC, play-money tokens). Content scripts and telemetry MUST detect the active currency toggle. Never fire real-money cashout goals, financial loss warnings, or drawdown alerts when GC / free-play mode is active.
- **Iframe & Frame Penetration:** Slot games almost universally render inside nested same-origin or cross-origin iframes. `manifest.json` `content_scripts` MUST specify `"all_frames": true`, and spin button selectors must resolve across iframe boundaries.
- **Default Bet Hazard on Game Load:** Slot providers frequently initialize sessions with inflated stakes ($1.00–$2.00) rather than minimum bets ($0.10–$0.20). Protect bankroll by maintaining the Default Bet Breaker check on first spin after page load, reload, or SPA game switch.
- **Cashier & Wallet Route Invariants:** Stake wallet modal links must use `?modal=wallet&tab=withdraw` (Stake.com) and `?modal=wallet&tab=redeem` (Stake.us). Never invert to `tab=wallet&modal=withdraw`, which causes the Stake frontend router to hang with an infinite spinner.

## Extension Popup UI & Component Invariants

- **Zero Unwired UI Elements:** Never introduce an interactive control (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<a>`) in `popup.html` without immediately defining and attaching an active, non-throwing event listener in `popup.ts`.
- **Icon Semantic Standards:** Use standard, universally recognized glyphs on a unified 24x24 viewBox (e.g., standard 6-tooth mechanical cog for settings; `help-circle` question mark for tutorials/onboarding; external link for window popouts). Never use sun/brightness icons for settings.

## Quick pass/fail check

- [ ] Untrusted data is validated/sanitized before use
- [ ] Extension boundary changes are explicit and minimally privileged
- [ ] Accessibility and failure-state behavior are covered
- [ ] Sweepstakes GC/SC currency modes are distinguished before alerts trigger
- [ ] Every interactive control in popup.html has an active listener in popup.ts
- [ ] All frames (`all_frames: true`) are covered for slot iframe click throttling
